            <ArticleTitle>[The results of the Lichtenstein's hernioplasty].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>30-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The study assumes the results of 1010 Lichtenstein's hernioplasties. The goal of the investigation was to estimate the results in dependence of the type of the polypropylene implant. The &quot;lite&quot; mesh was used in 342 cases, the second group of 668 patients had the so called &quot;heavy&quot; mesh endoprosthesis. Comparing the early postoperative period, it was registered, that the patients of the 2nd group had statistically higher rates of wound inflammatory infiltrate - 2.7% in comparison with 0.6% for the 1st group. The late postoperative period was marked by the higher rate of neuralgia among the &quot;heavy&quot; group - 5.2% in comparison with 1.5% for the &quot;lite&quot; group. Thus, the use of &quot;lite&quot; mesh polypropylene implant proved to be much more preferable for the Lichtenstein's hernioplasty.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
